Z||000000||Standard||08-21-2000||12:12 AM||||I'm just wondering if anyone has any suggestions on a good spot to splice into the wiring for the door switches to use the DFS alarm on my pioneer.. thanks in advance!<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 149,000 miles and counting!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||08-21-2000||06:15 AM||||Anyone?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||08-21-2000||08:23 AM||||Does it have to be ground contact, or a positive contact?||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||08-21-2000||09:22 AM||||When I re-wired my car alarm, I believe the installation shop used a white wire behind the guage console for the door pin switches. You have to take off the plastic rear cover held on by 5 torx screws. Then near the headlight switch will be a white wire. Just spice into that.<P>Note: turning on the dome light will also set off the alarm when it is armed, if wired this way.||||reg||1
Z||000004||cifc||08-21-2000||12:37 PM||||The easiest place to get your door trigger wire is at the underdash light.  Just tap into the white wire.<BR>--Jason<p>[This message has been edited by cifc (edited 08-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||08-23-2000||04:51 AM||||Cool, thanks a bunch guys!  Now i just gotta find some time to wire it up.  The DFS alarm is only armed when the face of the stereo is off..<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 149,000 miles and counting!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
